{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Operator decision 2026-11-02 (final): set receive.checkReferencedObjectsAreReachable = false on the production Gerrit, through infra/ (infra/compose/gerrit.config, the gerrit.config receive.* key per Gerrit's config-gerrit docs; jgit.config holds JGit-native keys like receive.autogc). Rationale: the confirmed mechanism is JGit FullConnectivityChecker rejecting thin-pack external delta bases taken from other open changes when the client's gerrit/main is stale; --no-thin is ignored over HTTPS, so no client flag fixes it. Accepted trade-off: Gerrit docs say to disable this check only if clients are trusted not to forge SHA-1 references to reach commits hidden from them. The operator accepts this because every client of this Gerrit is the shared bot account. No client-side no-delta packing workaround is adopted."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1793642927675171001,"uuid":"e335d9ef-a89f-4e57-8347-52292625afcd"}